WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:01.033
- So I couldn't help but notice,

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.933
that in your new lovely book,

00:00:02.933 --> 00:00:05.595
it started here, like after you were here.

00:00:05.595 --> 00:00:07.393
- It did, we were right
over there cooking.

00:00:07.393 --> 00:00:08.226
- I know.

00:00:08.226 --> 00:00:09.205
Making a crab and cheesy dip.

00:00:09.205 --> 00:00:10.615
- Which I don't cook well,
but I love the discernment.

00:00:10.615 --> 00:00:11.448
- You made that great dip.

00:00:11.448 --> 00:00:12.281
(giggles)

00:00:12.281 --> 00:00:13.114
- Because of you.

00:00:13.114 --> 00:00:13.947
(giggling simultaneously)

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:15.918
- And then, oh yes, there we are.

00:00:15.918 --> 00:00:18.339
And then I took the
leftovers 'cause I always,

00:00:18.339 --> 00:00:19.448
you know have stuff at home too,

00:00:19.448 --> 00:00:20.681
because I'm always
practicing before I do it.

00:00:20.681 --> 00:00:22.293
And I took it over to Wolfe's house

00:00:22.293 --> 00:00:23.592
and that's when Ed came by,

00:00:23.592 --> 00:00:26.093
and it all starts the whole story of

00:00:26.093 --> 00:00:27.529
this reconnection that Ed and I had

00:00:27.529 --> 00:00:29.389
in the last few years of his life.

00:00:29.389 --> 00:00:30.222
- Oh, wow.

00:00:30.222 --> 00:00:31.055
- Yeah.

00:00:31.055 --> 00:00:32.100
- That must have been hard.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.789
I know because I've
gone through a divorce,

00:00:33.789 --> 00:00:34.897
still going through divorce,

00:00:34.897 --> 00:00:35.969
and it's like, it feels,

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:38.739
it's a weird thing, but
it feels like a death.

00:00:38.739 --> 00:00:39.572
- Yeah.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.878
- Like it feels like such a loss,

00:00:40.878 --> 00:00:42.064
like divorce in general,

00:00:42.064 --> 00:00:44.287
and then to lose him again,
that must have been really hard.

00:00:44.287 --> 00:00:45.120
- Yeah, it sucks.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.601
- 'Cause it's your kid's
father too, you know?

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:48.434
Yeah.

00:00:48.434 --> 00:00:49.944
- Yeah, but there was something,

00:00:49.944 --> 00:00:51.594
and I know so many people get mad at me

00:00:51.594 --> 00:00:53.914
when I say that there was a love that Ed

00:00:53.914 --> 00:00:55.424
and I had that no one really can.

00:00:55.424 --> 00:00:56.546
And it's, but it's true.

00:00:56.546 --> 00:00:57.379
I mean, I don't know why was it.

00:00:57.379 --> 00:00:58.216
- Why do they get mad,

00:00:58.216 --> 00:00:59.295
but that's a beautiful thing?

00:00:59.295 --> 00:01:01.626
- Because we were both
married to other people.

00:01:01.626 --> 00:01:02.459
But it wasn't,

00:01:02.459 --> 00:01:03.919
it was nothing sexual.

00:01:03.919 --> 00:01:04.858
It was nothing.

00:01:04.858 --> 00:01:07.699
It was just, I've known the
guy since I was 20 years old.

00:01:07.699 --> 00:01:08.755
I was a baby,

00:01:08.755 --> 00:01:12.194
and he was just my life
for a very long time.

00:01:12.194 --> 00:01:13.732
So I'm a little uncomfortable
talking about it,

00:01:13.732 --> 00:01:16.073
but I'm not because there's
nothing to be ashamed of

00:01:16.073 --> 00:01:17.222
when you love somebody.

00:01:17.222 --> 00:01:18.055
- Yeah.

00:01:18.055 --> 00:01:18.888
- Love is love.

00:01:18.888 --> 00:01:19.890
- I think there's room
to love a lot of people

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.902
and there are different types of love.

00:01:21.902 --> 00:01:22.735
- Yes, yes.

00:01:22.735 --> 00:01:23.568
- Yeah. Oh.

00:01:23.568 --> 00:01:24.987
- And it turned into like brother, sister

00:01:24.987 --> 00:01:26.756
and I care about him so much.

00:01:26.756 --> 00:01:27.589
Still do.

00:01:27.589 --> 00:01:28.422
- Yeah.

00:01:28.422 --> 00:01:29.255
- Still do.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.053
Why did you call the
book "Enough Already"?

00:01:31.053 --> 00:01:31.886
And it's,

00:01:31.886 --> 00:01:35.249
I love that "Learning to
love the way I am today".

00:01:35.249 --> 00:01:37.615
- Because, I'm done.

00:01:37.615 --> 00:01:38.824
I'm just done judging myself.

00:01:38.824 --> 00:01:41.205
I'm done with all the
negative talk that I give

00:01:41.205 --> 00:01:43.486
to myself because there's
enough negative talk out there.

00:01:43.486 --> 00:01:44.635
It's just enough already, enough.

00:01:44.635 --> 00:01:46.123
Enough getting on the scale,

00:01:46.123 --> 00:01:47.347
enough saying horrible
things about myself.

00:01:47.347 --> 00:01:48.180
- Yeah.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.424
- And just changing the perspective,

00:01:50.424 --> 00:01:51.336
and changing,

00:01:51.336 --> 00:01:52.169
- The narrative.

00:01:52.169 --> 00:01:53.478
- The view and the narrative, thank you.

00:01:53.478 --> 00:01:55.729
And also, I am enough.

00:01:55.729 --> 00:01:56.562
I'm enough.

00:01:56.562 --> 00:01:57.478
- Yeah.

00:01:57.478 --> 00:01:58.311
- It's enough.

00:01:58.311 --> 00:01:59.248
- It's so interesting,

00:01:59.248 --> 00:02:01.219
'cause from an outsider's
perspective and just even

00:02:01.219 --> 00:02:03.872
having the one lunch we got
to share, like it was like

00:02:03.872 --> 00:02:06.261
I literally remember
leaving and telling Ashley,

00:02:06.261 --> 00:02:07.923
I was like, man, she is such a light.

00:02:07.923 --> 00:02:08.756
She's so kind.

00:02:08.756 --> 00:02:09.883
She's so normal.

00:02:09.883 --> 00:02:10.933
You were so cool.

00:02:10.933 --> 00:02:11.766
Like rarely

00:02:11.766 --> 00:02:13.213
- I thought the same thing about you.

00:02:13.213 --> 00:02:15.240
- Well what's funny is, rarely
do you meet people like,

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.336
- In this business.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:17.797
- You know, we're always working

00:02:17.797 --> 00:02:20.224
and busy, busy and rarely
do I really find that.

00:02:20.224 --> 00:02:24.391
And so I had advice actually
given to me for 2022.

00:02:25.362 --> 00:02:28.722
And it was like treat
yourself how you treat other.

00:02:28.722 --> 00:02:31.111
Oh no, yes treat yourself
how you treat others.

00:02:31.111 --> 00:02:33.423
And it's like, 'cause
I feel like we are kind

00:02:33.423 --> 00:02:36.149
to people a lot often
more than to ourselves.

00:02:36.149 --> 00:02:37.024
- Yes, unfortunately

00:02:37.024 --> 00:02:37.957
- Which so crappy.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:38.790
- Right.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:39.623
And it's not okay.

00:02:39.623 --> 00:02:40.456
- Why do we do that?

00:02:40.456 --> 00:02:41.289
- I don't know

00:02:41.289 --> 00:02:42.879
I mean, it's just, I
learned from a very, very

00:02:42.879 --> 00:02:44.719
very young age by, you
know, just the way you watch

00:02:44.719 --> 00:02:46.870
and the way you see the way
people treat each other.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:49.561
That it's just the certain
things that you're allowed to say

00:02:49.561 --> 00:02:52.047
and not allowed to say
and not allowed to feel.

00:02:52.047 --> 00:02:53.910
And I learned at a young age that,

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:56.620
gaining weight was
unlovable, made me unlovable.

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:57.453
- Wow.

00:02:57.453 --> 00:02:59.189
- So I'm still trying to purge

00:02:59.189 --> 00:03:01.489
that out of my system because
it's not, that's not true.

00:03:01.489 --> 00:03:02.430
It's just a lie.

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:03.750
- No, yeah, that's,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.887
oh my gosh that's so sad.

00:03:04.887 --> 00:03:06.605
I think that's a thing in the
South that said a lot too.

00:03:06.605 --> 00:03:07.446
- Everywhere.

00:03:07.446 --> 00:03:08.279
- I don't know if its everywhere.

00:03:08.279 --> 00:03:09.112
- All over the world.

00:03:09.112 --> 00:03:09.945
- Yeah.

00:03:09.945 --> 00:03:10.789
That's definitely in the South.

00:03:10.789 --> 00:03:11.853
But I, also I think what

00:03:11.853 --> 00:03:13.491
I am glad about is,

00:03:13.491 --> 00:03:16.312
I think so many things
happened to me when I was young

00:03:16.312 --> 00:03:19.190
about my weight that I think
like even at a young age,

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:20.023
like so many things get said,

00:03:20.023 --> 00:03:22.668
that I think that's whenever
I was just like, whatever

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:23.980
I'm not gonna please anyone.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:24.813
- God bless you.

00:03:24.813 --> 00:03:26.561
- I think I was lucky
it happened because it

00:03:26.561 --> 00:03:28.340
before I got in the
industry, because it was like

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.670
'cause it literal in the industry.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:30.878
You're talking about your
son being in the industry.

00:03:30.878 --> 00:03:31.711
It's very hard.

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:32.544
Even for men.

00:03:32.544 --> 00:03:33.377
- Yes.

00:03:33.377 --> 00:03:34.210
- Even for men.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.043
- Yes.

00:03:35.043 --> 00:03:36.418
- To look a certain way
and do with certain things

00:03:36.418 --> 00:03:37.829
and it's, and it's just
such a silly thing.

00:03:37.829 --> 00:03:39.279
And I love the title.

00:03:39.279 --> 00:03:40.112
- Thank you.

00:03:40.112 --> 00:03:40.945
- "Enough Already".

00:03:40.945 --> 00:03:42.680
'Cause it's very, welcoming

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.861
to so many people that have the same fight

00:03:44.861 --> 00:03:45.708
within themselves.

00:03:45.708 --> 00:03:46.774
- That they're trying to overcome.

00:03:46.774 --> 00:03:48.064
- It's hard when you learn

00:03:48.064 --> 00:03:50.224
as a little girl and then
trying to get that out.

00:03:50.224 --> 00:03:52.507
So for you to break that as a little girl.

00:03:52.507 --> 00:03:53.340
- Yeah.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:54.685
- Is something to be really proud of.

00:03:54.685 --> 00:03:55.614
It took me a long time.

00:03:55.614 --> 00:03:57.324
I mean I watched my mom not get loved

00:03:57.324 --> 00:03:58.736
by my dad when she would gain weight.

00:03:58.736 --> 00:03:59.569
- Oh God!

00:03:59.569 --> 00:04:01.555
- I had an elementary school teacher point

00:04:01.555 --> 00:04:03.235
at my belly and say,
"you better watch that".

00:04:03.235 --> 00:04:05.467
And I didn't even realize
I had a body before that.

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:07.747
Like I had no awareness
of what I looked like.

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:08.834
It was just like, let's have fun.

00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:10.786
And then all of a sudden I was like,

00:04:10.786 --> 00:04:12.011
oh I'm supposed to look a certain way?

00:04:12.011 --> 00:04:12.844
- Oh!

00:04:12.844 --> 00:04:13.677
- Yeah, that's damaging.

00:04:13.677 --> 00:04:14.723
- That's not okay.

00:04:14.723 --> 00:04:15.556
- Yeah.

00:04:15.556 --> 00:04:17.624
No you gotta be so careful with what you

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:18.457
say in front of the little
ones, they're sponges

